# TeX packages the LuaLaTeX recipes read. TeX Live installs its infrastructure
# only by default, which leaves no `lualatex` on PATH; Quarto then asks tlmgr
# for a package named `lualatex`, which does not exist, and the build fails.
#
# The list below is derived rather than guessed: every source in src/ was
# compiled through both the Quarto and the vanilla Pandoc LuaLaTeX recipe under
# `lualatex -recorder`, and each file the runs opened was mapped back to the
# TeX Live package owning it.
#
# The derivation ran against TeX Live 2024, so names are checked against the
# current tlnet database before being listed here: l3backend was folded into
# l3kernel, which is why its files appear in the recording but not below.
#
# selnolig is deliberately absent. Pandoc's template loads it whenever `lang`
# metadata is present, and `pixi run setup` stages a pinned CTAN copy into
# .cache/texmf for exactly the minimal installations this list describes.

